A leap year is divisible by 4, except century years, which must be divisible by 400. A `@staticmethod` is fine here because it needs neither `self` nor `cls`.

```python
class Calendar:
    @staticmethod
    def is_leap_year(year):
        return year % 4 == 0 and (year % 100 != 0 or year % 400 == 0)

print(Calendar.is_leap_year(2024))   # True
print(Calendar.is_leap_year(1900))   # False
print(Calendar.is_leap_year(2000))   # True
```

The standard library also has `calendar.isleap(year)`.

